Data that is not part of this repository

  Face tracking models (MediaPipe, ICT-FaceKit and others) are downloaded at
  run time and keep their own licenses. The tracker reports which models allow
  commercial use.

Models the default tracker (facemesh) uses, all commercially usable

  MediaPipe Face Landmarker   Google, Apache-2.0
    https://storage.googleapis.com/mediapipe-models/face_landmarker/
    The face_landmarker.task bundle holds the face detector, FaceMesh-V2 and
    Blendshapes V2. Yorishiro changes their format, not their weights:
    - face detector: tflite2onnx to ONNX, then pnnx to ncnn
      (tracker/tools/export_mediapipe.py, a channel Pad op is rewritten
      for ncnn).
    - FaceMesh-V2: the ONNX conversion from PINTO model zoo 410_FaceMeshV2
      (Apache-2.0, https://github.com/PINTO0309/PINTO_model_zoo), then pnnx
      to ncnn.
    - Blendshapes V2: converted to ONNX by tracker/tools/mixer_tflite_to_onnx.py
      (fp16 weights stored as fp32, 1x1 convolutions as MatMul).
    Training data per Google's model cards: FaceMesh-V2 on Google's own
    smartphone photos taken through an AR app, depth from synthetic data;
    Blendshapes V2 on samples generated from multi-view lab captures fitted
    with Google's GHUM face model. The data is not distributed.
  ICT-FaceKit                 USC Institute for Creative Technologies, MIT
    https://github.com/ICT-VGL/ICT-FaceKit
    Neutral head and 53 ARKit-named expression shapes, used by the expression
    solver and the preview avatar.
  Eye openness model          Yorishiro, same license as the tracker
    tracker/src/yorishiro_tracker/assets/eye_openness.onnx, part of this
    repository. Trained only on synthetic renders of the ICT-FaceKit head
    (tracker/tools/eye_synth), eye crops located by FaceMesh-V2. No photos of
    real people were used for training; the user's own clips and CREMA-D were
    used for evaluation only.

Code adapted from MediaPipe (Apache-2.0)

  tracker/src/yorishiro_tracker/adapters/landmark_smoother.py follows
  MediaPipe's LandmarksSmoothingCalculator and OneEuroFilter and uses the
  Face Landmarker's smoothing settings. adapters/mediapipe_blendshapes.py
  copies the landmark subset and output order of face_blendshapes_graph.cc.
  mediapipe_ncnn/ reimplements MediaPipe's face detector decoding and
  landmark ROI handling. Copyright Google LLC, Apache-2.0.

Evaluation only, not used by the tracker and not distributed

  OpenSeeFace (BSD-2-Clause) and Intel Open Model Zoo models (Apache-2.0) run
  in their own environments for comparison (tracker/tools/osf_worker.py,
  tracker/tools/omz_worker.py). Research datasets (for example CREMA-D, ODbL)
  are used for evaluation only, never for training (see the tracker's
  design notes).
  Live2D sample models and the Live2D Cubism SDK are not included and are not
  redistributed. Users download them and accept Live2D's terms themselves.
  Yorishiro renders Live2D models with Ayagami and does not ship Live2D Cubism
  Core.

